  "summary": "The direct applications of paired-positive/negative representation learning, i.e. contrastive learning, to road-traffic-flow prediction are [V0237], [V0240], [V0239], and [V0238]. [V0237] is the strongest match: it uses MetroFlow and reports accuracy 0.93. [V0240] reports F1 0.79 from LedgerGuard, [V0239] reports AUROC 0.72 on AgriSat-4, and [V0238] reports MAE 0.65 on Atlas-ICU; these are direct by stated method and topic, though several dataset names are not traffic-specific. Prior-work-only mentions such as [V0197], [V0201], [V0061], and [V0170] were not counted as applications. Because exactly five IDs are required, [V0221] is listed fifth only as a non-contrastive road-traffic-flow comparator using self-attention on MetroFlow with accuracy 0.84, not as evidence for contrastive learning.",
